{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790489826,"nonce":"/5g9uxnO1ZGLaO2f54v2MEP28tw=","title":"Python: a dynamic item store out of range writes slot 0; an array's message says list","message":"def stores(xs, i, v):\n    try:\n        xs[i] = v\n    except IndexError as e:\n        print(e)\na = [1, 2, 3]\nstores(a, 5, 7)\nprint(a)          # CPython [1, 2, 3], zypy [7, 2, 3]\nstores(array.array('d', [1.0]), 2, 1.0)   # CPython 'array assignment index out of range', zypy says list\n\nWhen xs is dynamic (an Object parameter) the store goes through zb_any_setitem_i64: after the failed index check raises, the store still runs at index 0. The typed paths check and leave before the slot is written; the dynamic setitem should do the same, and name the array kind in its messages.","files":null}]}